org.freedesktop.Platform and its extensions, as published on Flathub

The runtime is built by the Freedesktop SDK project and distributed by
Flathub. It is an aggregate of several hundred free software components, each
under its own license; among them are the GNU C library (LGPL), GCC's runtime
libraries (GPL with the GCC runtime library exception), Mesa (MIT) and many
GPL, LGPL, MIT, BSD, Apache and MPL licensed libraries and tools.

This build mirrors the runtime at a pinned commit and installs it unchanged.
It does not unpack or inspect it, and the runtime's manifest.json names its
components but not their licenses, so the individual licenses are not listed
or checked here, and INCOMPATIBLE_LICENSE cannot apply to them.

The licenses of the components are recorded in the Freedesktop SDK sources,
one element per component:

  https://gitlab.com/freedesktop-sdk/freedesktop-sdk

The release branch matches the runtime branch (for example release/25.08).
The runtime's /usr/manifest.json lists the components and versions it was
built from.
